# Changelog entries are `changelog.d/` fragments now (see its README), so
# feature PRs no longer edit CHANGELOG.md. `union` stays as a backstop for the
# rare hand edit: GitHub's PR merge ignores it, but a local rebase/merge uses it.
#
# Two branches appending their own bullets under `## [Unreleased]` is the
# single most common conflict in this repo, and it is never a real one — the
# sides touch adjacent lines, not the same one. `union` keeps both.
#
# It is a resolve-then-eyeball tool, not a silent fix: bullets can interleave
# oddly and a section heading (`### Fixed`) can end up duplicated when both
# sides opened one. Read the merged `[Unreleased]` block before committing and
# fold any duplicate headings together.
CHANGELOG.md merge=union
